# Angular Development Rules

## Project Context
This is an Angular 18+ project with:
- Standalone components
- Server-Side Rendering (SSR)
- Zoneless change detection
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS 4 for styling

## Code Style & Best Practices

### Angular Components
- Use standalone components by default
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use OnPush change detection strategy when possible
- Keep components focused and single-responsibility
- Use reactive forms over template-driven forms
- Implement proper TypeScript typing
- **NEVER use "Component" suffix in class names** - Use descriptive names like `TaskListView`, `CalendarView`, `UserProfile` instead of `TaskListViewComponent`, `CalendarViewComponent`, `UserProfileComponent`

### File Organization
- One component per file
- Use barrel exports (index.ts) for clean imports
- Group related files in feature modules
- Keep services in a dedicated services folder

### TypeScript
- Use strict mode
- Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes
- Use proper typing for all variables and functions
- Avoid `any` type, use `unknown` or proper typing instead

### CSS/Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS 4 utility classes for styling
- Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS when possible
- Use CSS custom properties for theming when needed
- Follow Tailwind's design system and spacing scale
- Keep custom CSS minimal and component-scoped when necessary
- Use Tailwind's responsive design utilities (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:, 2xl:)
- Leverage Tailwind's color palette and design tokens

### Performance
- Use OnPush change detection
- Implement lazy loading for routes
- Use trackBy functions in *ngFor
- Optimize bundle size with tree shaking

### Testing
- Write unit tests for components and services
- Use Angular Testing Utilities
- Mock external dependencies
- Aim for high test coverage

### Code Generation
- Use Angular CLI for generating components, services, etc.
- Follow Angular naming conventions
- Use proper file naming (kebab-case for files)

## Common Patterns

### Service Injection
```typescript
constructor(private service: MyService) {}
```

### Component Structure
```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-component',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule],
  templateUrl: './component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./component.css']
})
export class MyComponent implements OnInit {
  // Component logic
}
```

### Reactive Forms
```typescript
form = this.fb.group({
  field: ['', Validators.required]
});
```

## Avoid
- Using `any` type
- Mutating objects directly (use immutability)
- Heavy computations in templates
- Circular dependencies
- Deeply nested component hierarchies
- Inline styles in templates (use CSS classes)
- **Adding "Component" suffix to class names** - Use clean, descriptive names without redundant suffixes

## Security
- Sanitize user input
- Use Angular's built-in XSS protection
- Validate all form inputs
- Use HTTPS in production

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Add proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Test with screen readers
